Description: seafdav: reject deactivated users
 basic_auth_user only validates the password, so an account deactivated by an
 admin, or frozen after failed logins (FREEZE_USER_ON_LOGIN_FAILED), still
 authenticates over WebDAV.
Author: dionysius <dragon.dionysius@gmail.com>
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/haiwen/seafdav/commit/9e86f0bac2762ea50c386f6a8f35f6c85505bfc3
Forwarded: https://github.com/haiwen/seafdav/pull/103
Comment: upstream merged this into the 13.0 branch only; master and 14.0 lack it.
--- a/seafdav/wsgidav/dc/domain_controller.py
+++ b/seafdav/wsgidav/dc/domain_controller.py
@@ -116,6 +116,10 @@
             if session:
                 session.close()
 
+        if not user.is_active:
+            _logger.warning('User %s is deactivated', ccnet_email)
+            return False
+
